{
  "annotations": {
    "list": [
      {
        "builtIn": 1,
        "datasource": {
          "type": "datasource",
          "uid": "grafana"
        },
        "enable": true,
        "hide": true,
        "iconColor": "rgba(0, 211, 255, 1)",
        "name": "Annotations & Alerts",
        "type": "dashboard"
      }
    ]
  },
  "description": "Did my last push ship, and when. Four rows read top to bottom: what is live right now, what CI did with the commit, what Flux did with the image, and what the pods did with the manifest.\n\nThe CI row needs AERIE_REPO_OWNER and AERIE_REPO_NAME set in aerie-cluster-config (scripts/k3s/cluster-config.json, applied by Provision 4). Both are optional, so an installation that never sets them gets this dashboard with an empty CI row and everything else working - the variables at the top show 'unset' when that is what happened.\n\nVertical lines across every row are Flux reconciles, posted as Grafana annotations by the Provider/Alert pair in observability/config/notification/.",
  "editable": true,
  "fiscalYearStartMonth": 0,
  "graphTooltip": 1,
  "links": [],
  "panels": [
    {
      "id": 1,
      "type": "row",
      "title": "Now",
      "collapsed": false,
      "panels": [],
      "gridPos": {
        "h": 1,
        "w": 24,
        "x": 0,
        "y": 0
      }
    },
    {
      "id": 2,
      "type": "stat",
      "title": "Latest commit on main",
      "description": "The full 40-character SHA of the newest commit on main, from GitHub. Its first seven characters are the suffix publish.yml puts on every image tag, which is what makes the three panels to the right comparable to this one by eye. Reads over a fixed seven days rather than the dashboard's time range - a dashboard zoomed to the last hour should still be able to say what the newest commit is. Empty means AERIE_REPO_OWNER/AERIE_REPO_NAME are unset in aerie-cluster-config, or the GitHub datasource's token cannot read this repository.",
      "datasource": {
        "type": "grafana-github-datasource",
        "uid": "github"
      },
      "gridPos": {
        "h": 4,
        "w": 6,
        "x": 0,
        "y": 1
      },
      "timeFrom": "7d",
      "targets": [
        {
          "refId": "A",
          "datasource": {
            "type": "grafana-github-datasource",
            "uid": "github"
          },
          "queryType": "Commits",
          "owner": "$owner",
          "repository": "$repo",
          "options": {
            "gitRef": "main"
          }
        }
      ],
      "transformations": [
        {
          "id": "sortBy",
          "options": {
            "fields": {},
            "sort": [
              {
                "field": "committed_at",
                "desc": true
              }
            ]
          }
        },
        {
          "id": "limit",
          "options": {
            "limitField": 1
          }
        }
      ],
      "fieldConfig": {
        "defaults": {
          "color": {
            "mode": "fixed",
            "fixedColor": "text"
          },
          "mappings": []
        },
        "overrides": []
      },
      "options": {
        "reduceOptions": {
          "calcs": [
            "lastNotNull"
          ],
          "fields": "/^id$/",
          "values": false
        },
        "colorMode": "none",
        "graphMode": "none",
        "justifyMode": "auto",
        "orientation": "auto",
        "textMode": "value",
        "text": {
          "titleSize": 12,
          "valueSize": 14
        },
        "wideLayout": true,
        "showPercentChange": false,
        "percentChangeColorMode": "standard"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": 3,
      "type": "stat",
      "title": "ImagePolicy selects (api)",
      "description": "The tag image-reflector-controller has chosen for aerie-api, read from aerie_flux_image_policy_latest_tag - the kube-state-metrics CustomResourceState entry in observability/controllers/kube-prometheus-stack.yaml. Displayed as the series name rather than a value: the metric is a constant 1 and the answer is the label on it. If this disagrees with the commit on the left, the stall is before the cluster - CI, the registry push, or the 5m ImageRepository scan. No data here means the CustomResourceState config is not loaded, not that no tag is selected.",
      "datasource": {
        "type": "prometheus",
        "uid": "prometheus"
      },
      "gridPos": {
        "h": 4,
        "w": 5,
        "x": 6,
        "y": 1
      },
      "targets": [
        {
          "refId": "A",
          "datasource": {
            "type": "prometheus",
            "uid": "prometheus"
          },
          "expr": "aerie_flux_image_policy_latest_tag{name=\"aerie-api\"}",
          "editorMode": "code",
          "range": false,
          "instant": true,
          "legendFormat": "{{tag}}"
        }
      ],
      "fieldConfig": {
        "defaults": {
          "color": {
            "mode": "fixed",
            "fixedColor": "text"
          },
          "mappings": []
        },
        "overrides": []
      },
      "options": {
        "reduceOptions": {
          "calcs": [
            "lastNotNull"
          ],
          "fields": "",
          "values": false
        },
        "colorMode": "none",
        "graphMode": "none",
        "justifyMode": "auto",
        "orientation": "auto",
        "textMode": "name",
        "text": {
          "titleSize": 12,
          "valueSize": 22
        },
        "wideLayout": true,
        "showPercentChange": false,
        "percentChangeColorMode": "standard"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": 4,
      "type": "stat",
      "title": "api pods run",
      "description": "The tag actually serving traffic, taken from each running container's image spec. Two values here is a rollout in progress, not an error. If this disagrees with the ImagePolicy panel, the stall is inside the cluster - the tag commit to the site repo, the aerie-image-tags ConfigMap, or the apps Kustomization's 10m interval, in that order.",
      "datasource": {
        "type": "prometheus",
        "uid": "prometheus"
      },
      "gridPos": {
        "h": 4,
        "w": 5,
        "x": 11,
        "y": 1
      },
      "targets": [
        {
          "refId": "A",
          "datasource": {
            "type": "prometheus",
            "uid": "prometheus"
          },
          "expr": "count by (tag) (label_replace(kube_pod_container_info{namespace=\"aerie\", container=\"api\"}, \"tag\", \"$1\", \"image_spec\", \".*:(.+)\"))",
          "editorMode": "code",
          "range": false,
          "instant": true,
          "legendFormat": "{{tag}}"
        }
      ],
      "fieldConfig": {
        "defaults": {
          "color": {
            "mode": "fixed",
            "fixedColor": "text"
          },
          "mappings": []
        },
        "overrides": []
      },
      "options": {
        "reduceOptions": {
          "calcs": [
            "lastNotNull"
          ],
          "fields": "",
          "values": false
        },
        "colorMode": "none",
        "graphMode": "none",
        "justifyMode": "auto",
        "orientation": "auto",
        "textMode": "name",
        "text": {
          "titleSize": 12,
          "valueSize": 22
        },
        "wideLayout": true,
        "showPercentChange": false,
        "percentChangeColorMode": "standard"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": 5,
      "type": "stat",
      "title": "api on selected tag",
      "description": "The agree/disagree signal, as a fraction of running api containers whose image tag is the one the ImagePolicy selected. Green at 100%, orange mid-rollout, red when nothing running carries the selected tag.\n\nThis compares the cluster against itself and says nothing about whether the ImagePolicy is current - green here with a stale tag on the left is a build or registry-scan problem, and both halves have to agree before a commit is live.",
      "datasource": {
        "type": "prometheus",
        "uid": "prometheus"
      },
      "gridPos": {
        "h": 4,
        "w": 4,
        "x": 16,
        "y": 1
      },
      "targets": [
        {
          "refId": "A",
          "datasource": {
            "type": "prometheus",
            "uid": "prometheus"
          },
          "expr": "(count(\n  label_replace(kube_pod_container_info{namespace=\"aerie\", container=\"api\"}, \"tag\", \"$1\", \"image_spec\", \".*:(.+)\")\n  * on (tag) group_left ()\n  aerie_flux_image_policy_latest_tag{name=\"aerie-api\"}\n) or vector(0))\n/\ncount(kube_pod_container_info{namespace=\"aerie\", container=\"api\"})",
          "editorMode": "code",
          "range": false,
          "instant": true,
          "legendFormat": ""
        }
      ],
      "fieldConfig": {
        "defaults": {
          "unit": "percentunit",
          "min": 0,
          "max": 1,
          "decimals": 0,
          "color": {
            "mode": "thresholds"
          },
          "mappings": [],
          "thresholds": {
            "mode": "absolute",
            "steps": [
              {
                "color": "red",
                "value": null
              },
              {
                "color": "orange",
                "value": 0.01
              },
              {
                "color": "green",
                "value": 1
              }
            ]
          }
        },
        "overrides": []
      },
      "options": {
        "reduceOptions": {
          "calcs": [
            "lastNotNull"
          ],
          "fields": "",
          "values": false
        },
        "colorMode": "background",
        "graphMode": "none",
        "justifyMode": "auto",
        "orientation": "auto",
        "textMode": "auto",
        "wideLayout": true,
        "showPercentChange": false,
        "percentChangeColorMode": "standard"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": 6,
      "type": "stat",
      "title": "files on selected tag",
      "description": "The same fraction for the kiosk-files containers, against the kiosk-files ImagePolicy.",
      "datasource": {
        "type": "prometheus",
        "uid": "prometheus"
