    {
      "id": 36,
      "type": "stat",
      "title": "CNPG: newest base backup",
      "description": "Age of the newest completed CNPG Backup object, from its status.stoppedAt. Deliberately NOT cnpg_collector_last_available_backup_timestamp, which reads 0 forever under the barman-cloud plugin - see the CustomResourceState entry in kube-prometheus-stack.yaml. WAL archiving continues between base backups, so PITR is finer-grained than this number; what this measures is how far back the oldest recoverable point can reach.",
      "datasource": {
        "type": "prometheus",
        "uid": "prometheus"
      },
