    {
      "id": 37,
      "type": "stat",
      "title": "Longhorn: stalest volume",
      "description": "Age of the OLDEST of the three longhorn-r3 volume backups (Grafana, Uptime Kuma, Alertmanager) - the stalest volume rather than the newest, because the failure this is watching for is one volume being skipped while the other two succeed: Longhorn drops a detached volume from a recurring job with a warn log and a successful run. A volume that has never been backed up reports 0 for its last backup, so it shows here as an age of decades rather than as No data.",
